## PlaceGroups - Add Places [/external/v1/place_groups/{id}/add_places{?place_ids}]

This endpoint allows you to add places to a given place group. Place IDs are passed as
comma-separated IDs and the response data contains status as to whether or not places were
successfully added to the place group.

This method will always return a 200 and the status of adding individual
places to the given place group will be reported in the `data` response hash.

* `place_ids_added` - Places successfully added to given place group
* `place_ids_missing` - Given place IDs that do not exist
* `place_ids_existing` - Place IDs already in given place group


### Add places to PlaceGroup [PUT]

+ Parameters
    + place_ids (required, list of IDs, `3,4,5`) ... Place IDs to add to place group

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer 1234567890abcdef

    + Body

            {
                place_ids: "3,4,5"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "request":{
                "status_code":200,
                "status_message":"OK",
                "path":"/external/v1/place_groups/28/add_places",
                "method":"PUT",
                "params":{
                    "place_ids":"3,4,5"
                }
            },
            "data":{
                "place_ids_added":[3,4,5],
                "place_ids_missing":[],
                "place_ids_existing":[]
            }
        }

## PlaceGroups - Remove Places [/external/v1/place_groups/{id}/remove_places{?place_ids}]

This endpoint allows you to remove places from a given place group. Place IDs are passed as
comma-separated IDs and the response data contains status as to whether or not places were
successfully removed from the place group.

This method will always return a 200 and the status of removing individual
places from the given place group will be reported in the `data` response hash.

* `place_ids_removed` - Places successfully removed from given place group
* `place_ids_missing` - Given place IDs that do not exist


### Remove places from PlaceGroup [PUT]

+ Parameters
    + place_ids (required, list of IDs, `3,4,5`) ... Place IDs to remove from place group

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer 1234567890abcdef

    + Body

            {
                place_ids: "4,5,6"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "request":{
                "status_code":200,
                "status_message":"OK",
                "path":"/external/v1/place_groups/28/remove_places",
                "method":"PUT",
                "params":{
                    "place_ids":"4,5,6"
                }
            },
            "data":{
                "place_ids_removed":[4,5],
                "place_ids_missing":[6]
            }
        }


