## Teams - Add Users [/external/v1/teams/{id}/add_users{?user_ids}]

This endpoint allows you to add users to a given team. User IDs are passed as
comma-separated IDs and the response data contains status as to whether or not users were
successfully added to the team.

This method will always return a 200 and the status of adding individual
users to the given team will be reported in the `data` response hash.

* `user_ids_added` - Users successfully added to given taem
* `user_ids_missing` - Given user IDs that do not exist
* `user_ids_existing` - User IDs already in given team


### Add users to Team [PUT]

+ Parameters
    + user_ids (required, list of IDs, `3,4,5`) ... User IDs to add to team

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer 1234567890abcdef

    + Body

            {
                user_ids: "3,4,5"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "request":{
                "status_code":200,
                "status_message":"OK",
                "path":"/external/v1/teams/26/add_users",
                "method":"PUT",
                "params":{
                    "user_ids":"3,4,5"
                }
            },
            "data":{
                "user_ids_added":[5,4,3],
                "user_ids_missing":[],
                "user_ids_existing":[]
            }
        }

## Teams - Remove Users [/external/v1/teams/{id}/remove_users{?user_ids}]

This endpoint allows you to remove users from a given team. User IDs are passed as
comma-separated IDs and the response data contains status as to whether or not users were
successfully removed from the team.

This method will always return a 200 and the status of removing individual
users from the given team will be reported in the `data` response hash.

* `user_ids_removed` - User successfully removed from given team
* `user_ids_missing` - Given user IDs that do not exist


### Remove users from a Team [PUT]

+ Parameters
    + user_ids (required, list of IDs, `4,5,6`) ... User IDs to remove from team

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer 1234567890abcdef

    + Body

            {
                user_ids: "4,5,6"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "request":{
                "status_code":200,
                "status_message":"OK",
                "path":"/external/v1/teams/26/remove_users",
                "method":"PUT",
                "params":{
                    "user_ids":"4,5,6"
                }
            },
            "data":{
                "user_ids_removed":[5,4],
                "user_ids_missing":[6]
            }
        }


## Teams - Index Fields Filtering [/external/v1/teams?parent_id.eq=4]

The following are all of the fields available to filter and sort Teams for
your company. For explanations of matchers, please read the introduction on [index matchers](#intro-index-requests-matchers).

| Field                | Type           | Matchers                                   | Example                                   |
|----------------------|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|
| `name`               | string         | `.eq`, `.like`, `.ilike`, `.in`            | `name.eq=Company Managers`                |
| `id`                 | int            | `.eq`, `.gt`, `.gte`, `.lt`, `.lte`, `.in` | `id.eq=1`                                 |
| `created_at`         | unix timestamp | `.eq`, `.gt`, `.gte`, `.lt`, `.lte`        | `created_at.eq=1406236435.060687`         |
| `updated_at`         | unix timestamp | `.eq`, `.gt`, `.gte`, `.lt`, `.lte`        | `updated_at.eq=1406236435.060687`         |


# Group Missions
<a id="group-missions-index"></a>
The Missions endpoint allows you to list Missions for your company.

Remember:
- Missions are synonymous with campaigns throughout the API
- Missions are the surveys/audits that go to the mobile apps for reps to complete
- Missions contain sections, which contain tasks
- Calls will time out after 30 seconds, be sure to get small sets of data at a time to avoid hitting the timeout.

## Missions - Base Attributes
| Field                       | Type | Notes     | Matchers | Examples (With Limits) |
|-----------------------------|------|-----------|----------|------------------------|
|`id`                         |  int | Unique GSC id                   | `.eq`, `.in` | `id.eq=22`, `id.in=4,3,2` |
|`name`                       |  string  | Name of mission, not unique | `.eq`, `.in` | `name.eq=Company Mission`, `name.in=Mission` |
|`instructions`               |  string  | Open text field for displaying instructions to users in the mobile app   | N/A | Not Filterable. |
|`created_at`                 |  datetime | When this version of the mission was created in GSC      | `.eq`, `.gt`, `.gte`, `.lt`, `.lte` | `created_at.eq=1635283293`, `created_at.gt=1635283293&created_at.lt=1635628893` |
|`updated_at`                 |  datetime | When this version of the mission was last updated in GSC | `.eq`, `.lt`, `.lte`, `.gt`, `.gte` | `updated_at.eq=1635283293`, `updated_at.gt=1635283293&updated_at.lt=1635628893` |
|`maximum_responses_per_user` |  int  | Optional setting to limit the number of times an individual user can respond to a mission | N/A | Not Filterable. |
|`maximum_responses_per_location` |  int  | Optional setting to limit the number of times a mission can be completed at one place | N/A | Not Filterable. |
|`state`                      |  string  | Missions can either be in draft, published (started), stopped, completed, archived or versioned | `.eq` | `state.eq=completed` |
|`enable_user_assigned_places`|  boolean | Mission is only available to users at their assigned places        | `.eq` | `enable_user_assigned_places.eq=true` |
|`archived_at`                |  datetime | When this version of the mission was archived in GSC              | `.eq`, `.gt`, `.gte`, `.lt`, `.lte` | `archived_at.eq=1635283293`, `archived_at.gt=1635283293&archived_at.lt=1635628893` |
|`version_identifier`         |  int  | Unique identifier to link multiple versions of a mission together     | `.eq`, `.in` | `version_identifier.eq=4`, `version_identifier.in=3,5` |
|`version_number`             |  int  | Version of the mission, always 1 unless mission has been versioned    | `.eq`, `.gt`, `.gte`, `.lt`, `.lte` | `version_number.eq=11`, `version_number.gt=2&version_number.lt=9` |
|`updated_by_id`              |  int  | ID of GSC user who last updated this version of the mission           | `.eq`, `.gt`, `.gte`, `.lt`, `.lte`, `.in` | `updated_by_id.eq=1`, `updated_by_id.lt=5&updated_by_id.gt=1` |
|`created_by_id`              |  int  | ID of GSC user who created this version of the mission | `.eq` | `created_by_id.eq=1` |
|`started_by_id`              |  int  | ID of GSC user who last started this version of the mission | `.eq`, `.in` | `started_by_id.eq=5`, `started_by_id.in=1, 5` |
|`started_at`                 |  datetime | When this version of the mission was started (published) in GSC | `.eq`, `.gt`, `.gte`, `.lt`, `.lte` | `started_at.eq=1635283293`, `started_at.gt=1635283293&started_at.lt=1635628893` |
|`stopped_by_id`              |  int  | ID of GSC user who last stopped this version of the mission | N/A | Not Filterable. |
|`stopped_at`                 |  datetime | When this version of the mission was stopped (same as completed_at) in GSC | N/A | Not Filterable. |
|`archived_by_id`             |  int  | ID of GSC user who archived this version of the mission | N/A | `arhived_by_id.eq=22` |
|`completed_at`               |  datetime | When this version of the mission was stopped (same as stopped_at) in GSC | `.eq`, `.gt`, `.gte`, `.lt`, `.lte` | `completed_at.eq=1406236435.060687`, `completed_at.gt=1635283293&completed_at.lt=1635628893` |
|`metadata/properties`        |  string   | Custom key/value pairs, key must be created by GSC but values can be pulled from the API |


## Available Includes for Missions
For more info, see: [Includes & Methods](#section-includes-methods)

- `sections`
- `tasks`
- `teams`
- `place_groups`

## Available Methods for Missions
For more info, see: [Includes & Methods](#section-includes-methods)

- `company_id`
- `info_url` - a link available to a rep from within GSC mobile app to a reference webpage or file
- `allow_new_places` - whether mission can be completed at rep-added new places
- `anywhere_mission` - whether mission can be completed without an associated place

## Create Missions

The following attributes are permitted when creating a Mission. All other attributes will be ignored.

| Field                                     | Type           | Required|Note|
|-------------------------------------------|----------------|----------|---|
| `name`                                    | string         | Yes |
| `instructions`                            | string         | No  |
| `maximum_responses_per_user`              | int            | No   |
| `maximum_responses_per_location`          | int            | No    |
| `info_url`                                | string         | No      |
| `state`                                   | string         | No | May be one of `draft`, `published`, `completed`, `deleted` and `archived`. |
| `teams`                                   | array          | No| An array of embedded attribute hashes for teams
| `place_groups`                            | array          | No| An array of embedded attribute hashes for place_groups


### POST
#### Create A New Mission
##### [/external/v1/missions]

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer 1234567890abcdef

    + Body

            {
                "name": "A New Mission",
                "instructions": "Mission instructions",
                "maximum_responses_per_user": null,
                "maximum_responses_per_location": 5,
                "enable_user_assigned_places": true,
                "allow_offline": false,
                "teams": [
                    {
                        "team_id":2
                    },
                    {
                        "team_id":3
                    }
                ],
                "place_groups": [
                    {
                        "place_group_id": 1
                    }
                ]
            }

+ Response 201 (application/json)

