# Group MissionResponses
<a id="group-missionresponses-index"></a>
The MissionResponses endpoint allows you to list MissionResponses for your company.

Remember:
- Currently only read-only methods are available for MissionResponses.
- MissionResponses contain TaskResponses.
- MissionResponses are completed by users on the mobile device.
- Requests will timeout after 30 seconds. Remember to get small sets of data by imposing range limits when using .lt, .lte, .gt, or .gte. 

## MissionResponses - Base Attributes
| Field                       | Type | Notes   | Matcher | Example (With Range Limits) |
|-----------------------------|------|---------|---------|-----------------------------|
|`id`                         |  int  | Unique GSC id  | `.eq`, `.in` | `id.eq=1`, `id.in=1,2` |
|`campaign_id`                |  int  | Campaign/mission id to which the MissionResponse has been submitted | `.eq` | `campaign_id.eq=1234` |
|`place_id`                   |  int  | Unique GSC id of the place where the MissionResponse was completed | `.eq`, `.in` | `place_id.eq=5431`, `place_id.in=3, 1` |
|`user_id`                    |  int  | Unique GSC id of the user who submitted the MissionResponse | `.eq`, `.in` | `user_id.eq=444`, `user_id.in=4, 2` |
|`state`                      |  string  | An in-progress MissionResponse will appear as `null`; a submitted MissionResponse is `completed` | `.eq` | `state.eq=completed` |
|`created_at`                 |  datetime  | When MissionResponse was created on the server - will be the same as `started_at` if the user is online. Will be after `started_at` if the user is working offline. | `.eq`, `.lt`, `.lte`, `.gt`, `.gte` | `created_at.eq=1406236435`, `created_at.gt=1406236435&created_at.lt=1406236460` |
|`updated_at`                 |  datetime  | Last time the MissionResponse was updated on the server. | `.eq`, `.lt`, `.lte`, `.gt`, `.gte` | `updated_at.eq=1406236460`, `updated_at.gte=1406236460&updated_at.lte=1406236500` |
|`completed_at`               |  datetime  | The time at which the MissionResponse was submitted from the mobile app, regardless of whether the user was working offline. | `.eq`, `.gt`, `.gte`, `.lt`, `.lte` | `completed_at.eq=1406236500`, `completed_at.gt=1406236500&completed_at.lte=1406236700` |
|`started_at`                 |  datetime  | The time at which the MissionResponse was started on the mobile app, regardless of whether the user was working offline. | `.eq`, `.gt`, `.gte`, `.lt`, `.lte` | `started_at.eq=1406236500`, `started_at.gte=1406236500&completed_at.lt=1406238000` |
|`my_gsc_completed`           |  boolean   | Whether the MissionResponse was completed on the webapp My GSC `true` or the mobile app `false` | `.eq` | `my_gsc_completed.eq=true` |
|`expires_at`                 |  datetime  | The time at which the MissionResponse will expire on the mobile app. |  N/A | Not Filterable. |
|`coordinates`                |  array     | Lat/Long of the user’s device when they started the MissionResponse on the device. | N/A | Not Filterable. |
|`location_timestamp`         |  datetime  | Timestamp of `coordinates` | N/A | Not Filterable. | 
|`location_accuracy`          |  int       | Accuracy of `coordinates` - in meters | N/A | Not Filterable. |
|`completed_coordinates`      |  arrat     | Lat/Long of the user’s device when they submitted the MissionResponse from the device. | N/A | Not Filterable. |
|`metadata/properties`        |  string    | Custom key/value pairs, key must be created by GSC but values can be pulled from the API |


## Available Includes for MissionResponses
For more info, see: [Includes & Methods](#section-includes-methods)

- `task_responses`
- `place`
- `user`
- `campaign` or `mission` (synonymous)

## Available Methods for MissionResponses
For more info, see: [Includes & Methods](#section-includes-methods)

- `generated_share_url` **(NOTE: This will create a share URL for a mission response if one does not already exist)
- `deeplink_params` - Include the deeplink custom parameters associated with the mission response (if any)
    - For details on providing custom parameters in a Mission Response deeplink, view the Help Center article: [Deep Linking: Add Custom Values for Reporting and a Call Back URL](https://support.gospotcheck.com/hc/en-us/articles/11782816425239-Deep-Linking-Add-Custom-Values-for-Reporting-and-a-Call-Back-URL)

