# Group TaskResponses
<a id="group-taskresponses-index"></a>
The TaskResponses endpoint allows you to list TaskResponses for your company.

Remember:
- Tasks are in Missions
- Task Responses are in Mission Responses
- Requests will timeout after 30 seconds. Remember to get small sets of data by imposing range limits when using .lt, .lte, .gt, or .gte. 


NOTE: Currently only read-only methods are available for TaskResponses.

## TaskResponses - Base Attributes
| Field                       | Type | Notes     | Matcher | Example (With Range Limits) |
|-----------------------------|------|-----------|---------|-----------------------------|
|`id`                         |  bigint (64bit)  | Unique GSC id  | `.eq`, `.in` | `id.eq=22`, `id.in=4,3,2` |
|`mission_response_id`        |  int  | GSC MissionResponse id to which the task response belongs, there are typically many TaskResponses in a single MissionResponse | `.eq`, `.in` | `mission_response_id.eq=4545`, `mission_response_id.in=2` |
|`task_id`                    |  int  | The GSC task this response was the answer to  | `.eq`, `.in` | `task_id.eq=677`, `task_id.in=5,5,4` |
|`value`                      |  string  | Selected or entered text/numeric value entered by the rep on the mobile device | `.eq` | `value.eq=Yes` |
|`created_at`                 |  datetime  | The time at which the TaskResponse was created on the server | `.eq`, `.lt`, `.lte`, `.gt`, `.gte` | `created_at.eq=1635283293`, `created_at.gt=1635283293&created_at.lt=1635628893` |
|`updated_at`                 |  datetime  | The time at which the TaskResponse was last updated on the server | `.eq`, `.lt`, `.lte`, `.gt`, `.gte` | `updated_at.eq=1635628893`, `updated_at.gte=1635628893&udpated_at.lte=1635801693` |
|`type`                       |  string  | Task type - e.g. Yes/No | `.eq` | `type.eq=No` |
|`context`                    |  string  |  Searchable list (aka catalog item) that was selected in the parent task response  | `.eq` | `context.eq=Count` |


## Available Includes for TaskResponses
For more info, see: [Includes & Methods](#section-includes-methods)

- `task`
- `mission_response`

## Available Methods for TaskResponses
For more info, see: [Includes & Methods](#section-includes-methods)

- `array_wrapped_values` - Values are returned as an array
- `catalog_item_ids` - Include catalog item IDs for searchable list selections
- `context_id` - Include the context's catalog item ID

