# Group CustomViews
<a id="group-customviews-index"></a>
The CustomViews endpoint allows you to access custom data queries configured by the GoSpotCheck team. These are automatically available from the API as soon as the report is available in the webapp.

- The `index` action lists all of the currently available database views.
- The `show` action deviates from RESTful standards and executes the custom database query similar to any other index action.
- The `metadata` action returns all of the types and matchers for each column of the custom view.

## Available Includes for CustomViews
For more info, see: [Includes & Methods](#section-includes-methods)

- none

## CustomViews [/external/v1/custom_views]

### List all CustomViews for company [GET]

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer 1234567890abcdef

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "request": {
                "status_code": 200,
                "status_message": "OK",
                "path": "/external/v1/custom_views",
                "method": "GET",
                "format": "json",
                "params": {}
            },
            "paging": {
                "next_page": null,
                "current_page": 1,
                "previous_page": null,
                "per_page": 25,
                "total_pages": 1,
                "total_records": 1,
                "first_timestamp": 1433867800.676872,
                "last_timestamp": 1433867800.676872
            },
            "data": [
                {
                    "id": 3,
                    "created_at": "2015-06-09T12:36:40.676-04:00",
                    "updated_at": "2015-06-09T12:36:40.676-04:00",
                    "name": "User Assigned Places",
                    "description": "All User Assigned Places"
                }
            ]
        }



## CustomView Query [/external/v1/custom_views/{id}]

The CustomViews `show` action deviates from standard RESTful practices as it
fully executes the database view as if it was itself an `index` action. In fact, all
[behaviors, filters and options available to the index actions](#section-api-requests-index-requests)
on any other endpoint are valid for this action. In order to filter you must know
the column names and types for your custom view which you can obtain from the
[metadata action](#group-customviews-metadata) documented below.

### Request data from CustomView [GET]

+ Parameters
    + id  (required, integer, `3`) ... Request records for custom view 3

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer 1234567890abcdef

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "request": {
                "status_code": 200,
                "status_message": "OK",
                "path": "/external/v1/custom_views/3",
                "method": "GET",
                "format": "json",
                "params": {}
            },
            "paging": {
                "next_page": null,
                "current_page": 1,
                "previous_page": null,
                "per_page": 25,
                "total_pages": 1,
                "total_records": 1,
                "first_timestamp": null,
                "last_timestamp": null
            },
            "data": [
                {
                    "email": "wilma_admin@acme.com",
                    "place_name": "Monday Haven",
                    "address": "412 Cancer Pl",
                    "city": "Ashville",
                    "state": "NC",
                    "uap_id": 1,
                    "place_id": 48,
                    "user_id": 2,
                    "search_vector": "'412':4 'ashvill':7 'cancer':5 'haven':3 'monday':2 'pl':6 'wilma_admin@acme.com':1"
                }
            ]
        }


## CustomView Metadata [/external/v1/custom_views/{id}/metadata]
<a id="group-customviews-metadata"></a>

The `metadata` end point returns the types and matchers for each column in the custom view.
These matchers are used in filtering the query. Not all fields may have available matchers
depenging on the column type and those will be apparent in the results. If you have any questions
regarding custom views, please contact GoSpotCheck for more information.

### Request data from CustomView [GET]

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer 1234567890abcdef

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "request": {
                "status_code": 200,
                "status_message": "OK",
                "path": "/external/v1/custom_views/3/metadata",
                "method": "GET",
                "format": "json",
                "params": {}
            },
            "data": {
                "email": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "match": "eq|like|ilike|in"
                },
                "place_name": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "match": "eq|like|ilike|in"
                },
                "address": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "match": "eq|like|ilike|in"
                },
                "city": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "match": "eq|like|ilike|in"
                },
                "state": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "match": "eq|like|ilike|in"
                },
                "uap_id": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "match": "eq|gt|gte|lt|lte|in"
                },
                "place_id": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "match": "eq|gt|gte|lt|lte|in"
                },
                "user_id": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "match": "eq|gt|gte|lt|lte|in"
                },
                "search_vector": {
                    "type": "tsvector",
                    "match": ""
                }
            }
        }
# Group Catalogs
<a id="group-catalogs-index"></a>
The Catalogs endpoint allows you to add, update and list catalogs and their items for your company.

Remember:
- Catalogs hold Catalog Items
- Catalogs are assigned to a searchable list task in the webapp
- Catalogs display items as a searchable list in the mobile apps

## Catalogs - Base Attributes
| Field                    | Type | Notes   |
|-----------------------------|-----|-----------|
|`id`                     |  int  | Unique GSC id  |
|`name`                     |  string  | Name of catalog, must be unique |
|`created_at`                     |  datetime  | When catalog was created in GSC   |
|`updated_at`                     |  datetime  | When catalog was last updated in GSC |
|`disabled_at`                     |  datetime  | If catalog is disabled, field will display when it was disabled  |
|`metadata/properties`                     |  string  | Custom key/value pairs, key must be created by GSC but values can be pulled from the API |

## Available Includes for Catalogs
For more info, see: [Includes & Methods](#section-includes-methods)

- catalog_items **(WARNING: if your catalog includes more than 1,000 items, only use this include when requesting an individual catalog by name or id as this request will likely time out on a GET all catalogs request)**

## Available Methods for Catalogs
For more info, see: [Includes & Methods](#section-includes-methods)

- `company_id`

## Catalogs [/external/v1/catalogs]

