                    "updated_at": "2015-07-31T16:40:14.110-04:00",
                    "disabled_at": null,
                    "catalog_property": "Catalog Property Value ABC"
                }
            ]
        }

# Group Catalog Items
<a id="group-catalog-items-index"></a>
The Catalog Items endpoint allows you to add, update and destroy catalog items for your company.

Remember:
- Catalog Items live in a Catalog
- Catalog Items can only exist in one catalog, add multiple items if you need the same SKU/item across multiple catalogs. Match custom_id’s to tie them together when you export data.
- Catalogs are assigned to a searchable list task in the webapp
- Catalogs display items as a searchable list in the mobile apps

## Catalog Items - Base Attributes
| Field                    | Type | Notes   |
|-----------------------------|-----|-----------|
|`id`                     |  int  | Unique GSC id  |
|`name`                     |  string  | Name of catalog item, must be unique |
|`custom_id`                     |  string  | Optional field to hold a custom identifier for the item, could be your unique id or SKU |
|`created_at`                     |  datetime  | When catalog item was created in GSC   |
|`updated_at`                     |  datetime  | When catalog item was last updated in GSC |
|`position`                     |  int  | Position in which item will appear in mobile searchable list |
|`disabled_at`                     |  datetime  | If catalog item is disabled, field will display when it was disabled and item will not appear in a searchable list in the mobile app  |
|`metadata/properties`                     |  string  | Custom key/value pairs, key must be created by GSC but values can be pulled from the API |
|`barcode`                     |  string  | Optional field to hold a barcode for a catalog item |


## Catalog Items [/external/v1/catalogs/{catalog_id}/items]

### List all Catalog Items for a Catalog [GET]
NOTE: You must specify catalog id in path: /external/v1/catalogs/{catalog_id}/items

