## Photo Grid Webhook

_Please contact your GoSpotCheck Account Manager if you wish to configure the webhook._

A webhook push request can be sent when the IR photo grid has finshed processing, that will contain the photo_grid_id for use in this API endpoint.
This webhook supports OAuth2 client-credentials for authenticating against your API that will recieve the webhook request. The following information will be needed:

**Required Webhook oAuth2 Parameters:**

  - `client_id`: string identifier for the GSC application in the your OAuth2 system
  - `client_secret`: string secret known only to the GSC application and your OAuth2 server
  - `token_url`: string url the GSC application can use to request an OAuth2 token your server
  - `audience`: string representing the resource URI/server for which the access token is intended
  - `token_duration`: int number of minutes for which the token is expected to be valid. It strongly recommended to provide a leeway to this value, so the token is refreshed before it expires. e.g. Token is valid for 60 minutes. The token_duration should be set to 55minutes, to prevent expired tokens being used in requests.
  
**Optional Webhook OAuth2 Parameters:**
- `scopes`: []string optional list of scopes (permission) that our servers will append to the request for the access token.

**Photo Grid Complete Webhook Body**
> Fields marked as "DEPRECATED" may be removed in a future release
```
{
  "event_type": "photo_grid_tagged",
  "payload": {
    "photo_grid": {
      "id": int64,
      "external_id": string,
      "created_at": string, # ISO 8601 timestamp
      "metadata": {
        "mission_response": {
          "id": int64
        },
        "scene": {
          "type": string,
          "type_code": string
        },
        "task_response": {
          "id": int64
        }
      }
    },
    "image": {
      "url": string,
      "expiry": int64, # DEPRECATED
      "width": int, # 0 if no tags
      "height": int # 0 if no tags
    }
  }
}
```


**Photo Grid Complete Webhook Body Example**
```
{
  "event_type": "photo_grid_tagged",
  "payload": {
    "photo_grid": {
      "id": 127,
      "external_id": "c093c206-9aff-4354-8f3c-ecdc19a1b8e7",
      "created_at": "2023-12-01T01:06:12.870337Z",
      "metadata": {
        "mission_response": {
          "id": 196362300
        },
        "task_response": {
          "id": 4296362300
        },
        "scene": {
          "type": "Shelf Photo Grid",
          "type_code": "shelf_grid"
        },
      }
    },
    "image": {
      "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/shelfwise-images-prd/523269e0-1b26-45b2-a0b5-11d2b0f8e691/2.jpg?X-Goog-Algorithm=...",
      "expiry": 1701479361,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1080
    }
  }
}
```

# v2 Tags
<a id="v2-tags"></a>
The v2 tags endpoints all the retrieval of Image Rec tags

## Get Tags [GET]
  **Description** 
  This endpoint allows you to get the list of filenames for Image Rec tags

  **Url:** `/external/v2/companies/:id/image_rec/scene_types/:id/tags?start_time=:start_time&end_time=:end_time&page=:page&include_tag_edits=:include_tag_edits`

  **Request Body**
```
N/A
```

**Required:**

  - `companyId`: The id of the company the tags belong to.
  - `scene_type`: The `scene_type` of the tags. 
  - `start_time`: Unix timestamp that will be used to determine the beginning of the time range used to filter the request.
  - `end_time`: Unix timestamp that will be used to determine the end of the time range used to filter the request.

**Optional**

  - `page`:  The page being requested. If not set, the request will default to page 1.
  - `include_tag_edits`: `True` if the Tag Edits should be included in the response. If not set, the request will default `False`

**Example Url**
```
api.gospotcheck.com/external/v2/companies/2/image_rec/scene_types/2/tags?start_time=1593583200&end_time=159392880&page=1&include_tag_edits=True
```

**Return Body**
```
{
    "paginationResponse": {
        "currentPage": int,
        "perPage": int
    },
    "companyId": string,
    "sceneTypeId": string,
    "tagFiles": [
        {
            "url": string,
            "category": string,
            "startTime": string,
            "endTime": string
        }
}
```
**Parameters**

  - `paginationResponse`: Contains the pagination currentPage and perPage.
  - `currentPage`: The page being requested.
  - `perPage`: The number of tagFiles returned, per page. Max is 100
  - `companyId`: The id of the company that the tags belong to.
  - `sceneTypeId`: The id of the sceneType, of the tags.
  - `tagFiles`: An array of urls that contain files of tags.
  - `url`: A url that allows for the downloading of the gzipped csv. The url expires in 1 hour.
  - `category`: The category of the tags. Raw tags and tag edits are supported:
      - `CATEGORY_RAW_TAGS` - tags as returned by the Image Recognition Platform
      - `CATEGORY_TAG_EDITS` - legacy non-UPC-level tag edits
      - `CATEGORY_UPC_TAG_EDITS` - UPC Tag Edits
  - `startTime`: The beginning of the time range that the file represents.
  - `endTime`: The end of the time range that the file represents.

**Return Example Body**
```
{
    "paginationResponse": {
        "currentPage": 1,
        "perPage": 100
    },
    "companyId": "220",
    "sceneTypeId": "10",
    "tagFiles": [
        {
            "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/hifi-hotrod-dev/scene_type_id%3D10/scene_type_version%3D1.0.0/protobuf_full_name%3Dcom.reporting.hifi.scenetypes.coldbox.v1/company_id%3D220/file_format%3Dcsv/record_action%3Dinsert/evented_at_year%3D2020/evented_at_quarter%3D3/evented_at_month%3D07/evented_at_day%3D16/evented_at_hour%3D21/part-00000-1008075b-a301-4c7a-afbb-5d8de808aae5.c000.csv.gz?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=bifrost%40core-apps-dev-806e73.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20200824%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20200824T171506Z&X-Goog-Expires=3598&X-Goog-&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host",
            "category": "CATEGORY_RAW_TAGS",
            "startTime": "2020-07-16T21:00:00Z",
            "endTime": "2020-07-16T22:00:00Z"
        },
        {
            "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/hifi-hotrod-dev/scene_type_id%3D10/scene_type_version%3D1.0.0/protobuf_full_name%3Dcom.reporting.hifi.scenetypes.coldbox.v1/company_id%3D220/file_format%3Dcsv/record_action%3Dinsert/evented_at_year%3D2020/evented_at_quarter%3D3/evented_at_month%3D07/evented_at_day%3D16/evented_at_hour%3D21/part-00000-1008075b-a301-4c7a-afbb-5d8de808aae5.c000.csv.gz?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=bifrost%40core-apps-dev-806e73.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20200824%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20200824T171506Z&X-Goog-Expires=3598&X-Goog-&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host",
            "category": "CATEGORY_UPC_TAG_EDITS",
            "startTime": "2020-07-16T21:00:00Z",
            "endTime": "2020-07-16T22:00:00Z"
        }
}
```

In case of UPC tag edits, the file would only contain the edited tags. The tag_id values in the Tag Edits file will match some of the tag_ids in the Raw Tags file to identify which tags had been edited. 


**Errors**

***Note: The following receive an error code of 400.***

  - "page must be a number and can not be zero" Indicates the page given was a non number or was a zero.
  - "companyId invalid or not provided" Indicates the company id was not provided in the url.
  - “sceneTypeId invalid or not provided" indicates the scene type id was not provided in the url.
  - “start time is required” indicates the start time was not provided in the url.
  - “end time is required” indicates the end time was not provided in the url.
  - “start time can not be more than two years from present”: indicates start time is more than 2 years ago.
  - “end time can not be in the future”: indicates end time is in the future.
  - “end time can not be before start time”: indicates end time is before start time.
  

## Get Tags By Photo Grid ID [GET]
  **Description** 
  This endpoint allows you to get a paginated set of tags by a photo grid id.

  **Url:** `external/v2/companies/:company_id/image_rec/tags?photo_grid_id=:photo_grid_id&photo_grid_external_id=:photo_grid_external_id&offset=:offset&limit=:limit`

  **Request Body**
```
N/A
```

**Required Parameters:**

  - `company_id`: The id of the company the tags belong to.
  - **One Of**
    - `photo_grid_id`: The photo_grid_id that contains a set of tags, and a single generated “composite” image
    - `photo_grid_external_id`:  The photo_grid_external_id that contains a set of tags, and a single generated “composite” image

**Optional**

  - `offset`:  The offset of the result set to omit. This may be omitted for the first request, but it is recommended to always include it
  - `limit`:  The maximum results to return per page. This may also be omitted, and a default of 50 will be set for the request in that case. The maximum limit that can be requested is 250

**Example Url**
```
api.gospotcheck.com/external/v2/companies/28/image_rec/tags?photo_grid_id=44&offset=0&limit=200
```

**Return Body**

_Bounding boxes requires an additional subscription._
The `bounding_box` data will not be available unless an additional subscription has been adding to your account.

Please contact your GoSpotCheck Account Manager if you are interested in receiving bounding box data.

```
{
  "pagination_response": {
    "offset": int,
    "limit": int,
    "has_more": bool
  },
  "tags": [{
    "type": string,
    "created_at": string (timestamp),
    "values": dynamic object,
    "customer_list_values": dynamic object,
    "latest_tag_edit": {
      "type": string,
      "created_at": string (timestamp),
      "values": dynamic object,
    }
  }]
}
```
**Parameters**

  - `pagination_response`: Contains the pagination information
  - `offset`: The zero-based offset of the first item returned in the collection.
  - `limit`: The maximum number of entries to return. 
  - `tags`: The list of tags associated with the photogrid.
      - `latest_tag_edit` (optional): if the tag has been edited by a user the new edited values will appear here
      - `customer_list_values` (optional):  if configured, a Dynamic list of custom tag attributes pulled from a custom product list
      - `bounding_box` (optional): if enabled, 4 integer values representing the absolute position, in pixels, of the tag on the image. The image and its dimensions is provided with the photo grid in the `Get Photo Grids by Mission Response ID` API or via webhooks.
  - `type`: The type of tag.
  - `created_at`: The timestamp the tag was created 
  - `values`: Dynamic list of tag attributes


**Return Example Body**
```
{
  "pagination_response": {
    "offset": 0,
    "limit": 200,
    "has_more": false
  },
  "tags": [{
    "type": "shelf_product",
    "created_at": "2020-07-16T21:00:00Z",
    "values": {
      "brand": "GSC",
      "brand_family": "GSC",
      "classification": "Beer",
      "grid_index": 1,
      "guid": "0a00000a-0000-0aa0-0aaa-a00aa0000000",
